<title>POLAND: Polish lower house passes new customs law.</title>
<headline>Polish lower house passes new customs law.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lower house of Poland's parliament, the Sejm, on Friday passed a new customs law, adjusting Polish regulations to European Union and World Trade Organisation (WTO) standards.</p>
<p>The Sejm voted by 343 to one with 15 abstentions in favour of the law, which will simplify procedures, strengthen customs offices and their supervision prerogatives, as well as streamline commodity trade.</p>
<p>The new law, one of the necessary adjustments of the Polish legal system before joining the EU, will come into force in mid-1997 when all the executive regulations will be ready.</p>
</text>
